# .xal/gate-inputs — the declared input contract for scripts/check.sh (the process repo).
#
# Every gate in scripts/check.sh that needs something NOT in this repo declares it here,
# and .xal/check-gate-inputs.sh asserts that every workflow invoking that script supplies
# it. This file exists because the gate script cannot see its own callers: the first time a
# gate gained a dependency on the `claude` CLI, ci.yml did not install it, and the gate
# failed on its first CI run — the second occurrence of the same failure shape in four days.
# See spec/gate-discipline.md §4.
#
# Format:  id | detect | required-in-ci | caller-pattern | expires | description
#   detect          command:<name> | env:<VAR> | none   (how check.sh discovers it)
#   required-in-ci  yes = the gate FAILS when absent under CI=true; no = it skips
#   caller-pattern  ERE every caller workflow must match, `<workflow>:<ERE>` for one
#                   workflow only, or `-` for runner-provided
#   expires         ISO date YYYY-MM-DD, or `-` for an input that cannot expire. A
#                   caller-pattern naming `secrets.` must carry a real date: the checker
#                   refuses `-` there, because a secret has an expiry whether or not it
#                   is written down.
#
# Gates 1-4 and 6-7 need only bash, awk, grep, sed, find, diff and mktemp — all present on
# any runner, and deliberately so in a repo whose whole point is language neutrality. They
# are not inputs in the sense this file means: nothing has to be supplied for them to run.

claude-cli | command:claude | yes | npm install -g @anthropic-ai/claude-code | -     | The `claude` CLI, for gate 5 (`claude plugin validate --strict` on the marketplace and every plugin). Offline schema validation only — it never calls the API, so no credential is needed. THIS IS THE INPUT THAT ONCE BROKE CI ON ITS FIRST RUN.
jq         | command:jq     | yes | -                                       | -     | `jq`, for gate 9 (the reader evaluator's fixtures: scripts/reader-eval.sh reads a verdict with it). Provided by the ubuntu-latest runner image, so no workflow step is needed, and mandatory under CI=true.
